  "applies_to": {
    "confirmed": ["sehri_end", "iftar"],
    "explanation": "The IFB offset tables are headed সাহরী and ইফতার. Those are the two columns the source publishes."
  },
  "caveats": [
    "SCOPE: these offsets are published for sehri end and iftar. The source's own footnote (ক) states that deriving other districts' sehri, sunrise, Dhuhr, Asr and Maghrib by adding or subtracting from Dhaka can vary, and that in the northern districts in particular the Asr offset may need to be LARGER than the table gives. Do not apply these values to Asr in the north without further verification.",
    "SEHRI MARGIN: the source states a 3-minute precautionary margin is added to the sehri end time (সতর্কতামূলক ব্যবস্থা হিসেবে ৩ মিনিট যোগ করা হয়েছে). Published sehri end is therefore earlier than the astronomical value.",
    "IFTAR MARGIN: the source sets iftar 3 minutes after true sunset. A purely astronomical Maghrib will read earlier than IFB's published iftar. Measured 2026-07-30 for Dhaka: astronomical 18:43, IFB published 18:47.",
    "MADHHAB: IFB uses Hanafi Asr. Verified 2026-07-30 for Dhaka, IFB Asr 16:43, matching a Karachi-angles + Hanafi-Asr computation exactly. A Standard/Shafi'i Asr gives 15:28 for the same day, 75 minutes early for this audience. Note that 'Karachi method' refers to twilight angles and is independent of the Asr madhhab setting.",
    "AGE: the source document was last updated 2015-11-18. Confirm against a current IFB publication before treating any single value as authoritative.",
    "COVERAGE: 63 of Bangladesh's 64 districts. Joypurhat is absent from the source's offset tables and is recorded here as unknown rather than estimated."
  ],
